  "term": "olfactory sense organ",
  "definition": "An olfactory sense organ is a specialized structure used to detect chemical cues. In the supplied source, this refers to the vomeronasal organ in snakes, an auxiliary smell-related organ that helps detect prey-produced chemicals important for prey recognition and predatory behavior.",
